 - Only managers may delete tasks.
 - Archived projects reject all writes with 409 (reads still work).
 - A task ID that does not belong to the project in the path → 404.
+- Moving a task (`/move`) needs the same write rights on the source as editing
+  it (contributors only move their own tasks). The destination project must be
+  readable by the user (missing, other organization or not readable → 404), the
+  user must be a contributor or manager there (else 403), and an archived
+  destination → 409. The task keeps its ID, title, status and assignee; if the
+  assignee is not a contributor or manager of the destination → 400.
 
